total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.7.beta [86082170822e19ebb619c7f53c8fe54a6f8d3d2a]\n\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.beta (566ac71d7) - macOS Tahoe (26.5.0) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M3 (Apple9) - Apple M3 (8 threads) - 16.00 GiB memory - CoreAudio (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\n`JavaClassWrapper.create_sam_callback()` / `create_proxy()` return a Java proxy whose `equals()` is broken on Android. Calling it always returns `false` (even for `proxy.equals(proxy)`), and the JNI bridge silently swallows a `StackOverflowError` that's left behind in `JavaClassWrapper.get_exception()`.\n\n`adb logcat` shows a deeply recursive stack trace from inside the proxy's `InvocationHandler`. The same thing breaks anywhere `equals` is used implicitly: putting the proxy into a `HashMap` or `ConcurrentHashMap`, `Objects.equals`, JUnit `assertEquals`, and so on. Since GDScript never sees the exception itself (it just gets `false` back), the bug is invisible from the script side and the proxy still looks fine for normal SAM calls. Only the equality path is affected.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Download the MRP, open it in Godot, and export to Android (any recent device or emulator works).\n2. Launch the app.\n\nThe label displays:\n\nBUG REPRODUCED\nresult=0, exception=<JavaObject:java.lang.StackOverflowError ...>\n\nThe same string is also printed to `adb logcat` (`[MRP] equals returned: 0` / `[MRP] Pending Java exception: ...`), followed by the recursive Java stack trace.\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28107198/mrp.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":